Experiment 2 — Lexical Analyzer using LEX
Aim

To create a lexical analyzer that reads a C source code file and identifies keywords, identifiers, constants, operators, preprocessor directives, header files, and delimiters using FLEX and regular expressions.

Algorithm
Start the program.
Define regular expressions for different types of tokens.
Create the three sections of the FLEX file:
Definitions
Rules
C code
Define patterns for keywords, identifiers, numbers, operators, and delimiters.
Define rules to recognize preprocessor directives and header files.
Read the C source file.
Match each input lexeme with the appropriate pattern.
Print the corresponding token type.
Continue until the end of the file.
Stop.
Pseudocode
START

Define patterns for:
    Keywords
    Identifiers
    Numbers
    Operators
    Delimiters
    Preprocessor directives
    Header files

Read C source program

WHILE input is not finished:
    Read next lexeme

    IF lexeme is a keyword:
        Print "Keyword"

    ELSE IF lexeme is an identifier:
        Print "Identifier"

    ELSE IF lexeme is a number:
        Print "Number"

    ELSE IF lexeme is an operator:
        Print "Operator"

    ELSE IF lexeme is a delimiter:
        Print "Delimiter"

    ELSE IF lexeme is a preprocessor directive:
        Print "Preprocessor Directive"

    ELSE IF lexeme is a header file:
        Print "Header File"

    ELSE:
        Ignore lexeme

END WHILE

Print "End of file"

STOP
